ed Process\nDescription: It’s possible to add to a workpage, a wizard that is based on a guided process template that was created and deployed from SAP Build Process Automation service.  For more information, see How to Create a Wizard.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-10-31\nVersion: 2410B\n\n--- Record 2017 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhanced Page Builder\nDescription: The workpage editor has been enhanced with the following capabilities:    Widget context menu      Ability to move sections up and down    Section configuration menu    Show/hide section header      Accessibility support      For more information, see How to Build and Design a Workpage.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-10-31\nVersion: 2410B\n\n--- Record 2018 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Passive Certificate\nDescription: You can define a passive certificate in the SAML Trusted IDP screen.  The purpose of adding a passive certificate is to have a backup certificate in case the active certificate has expired, and to avoid system downtime.  After adding a passive certificate in the SAP BTP cockpit, administrators must manually copy the certificate into the Administration Console - Authentication & Authorization -  SAML Trusted IDPs.  For more information, see SAML Trusted IDPs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-10-31\nVersion: 2410B\n\n--- Record 2019 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support X.509-Based Authentication in Identity Provisioning\nDescription: An x.509-based authentication is now supported between the Identity Provisioning service and SAP Build Work Zone.   For more information, see Option1: Create a new tenant -step 3", "4-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-10-31\nVersion: 2410B\n\n--- Record 2019 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support X.509-Based Authentication in Identity Provisioning\nDescription: An x.509-based authentication is now supported between the Identity Provisioning service and SAP Build Work Zone.   For more information, see Option1: Create a new tenant -step 3.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-10-31\nVersion: 2410B\n\n--- Record 2020 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: App Finder Enhancements\nDescription: The App Finder has been enhanced with a new a new design and some additional features, such as displaying the apps in a list view, the possibility to search for catalogs, and the option to hide the catalogs side panel.   For more information, see How to Use the App Finder.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-10-31\nVersion: 2410B\n\n", "--- Record 1461 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pass-through B2B Transaction\nDescription: You can now create a pass-through B2B transaction capability, enabling data forwarding between trading partners without requiring additional configuration.  See: Creating a Pass-Through B2B Transaction  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-08\nValid as Of: 2025-02-08\nVersion: 2413\n\n--- Record 1462 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Data Center Availability\nDescription: Joule is now available in the Sydney, Australia data center of Microsoft Azure. For more information about data centers, see Data Centers Supported by Joule.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-07\nValid as Of: 2025-02-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1463 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SensitiveExecuteHanaCloudSqlStatement Command\nDescription: You can now use the new SensitiveExecuteHanaCloudSqlStatement command.  See SensitiveExecuteHanaCloudSqlStatement Command.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-06\nValid as Of: 2025-02-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1464 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New URL authentication method for AvT (Expserv) monitors\nDescription: You can now create AvT (Expserv) URL monitors for endpoints protected by oAuth2 client credentials.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-06\nValid as Of: 2025-02-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1465 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Tagging Overhaul\nDescription: You now have two new tag-class types available: Value-Set tag classes and Label tag classes. Existing tag classes need to be migrated. You can migrate by editing a tag class. For more information, see   , as well as the UI itself, where a detailed explanation of the migration is also available.  These updates also come with new /v2/tagclasses APIs, successor to /v1/tagclasses that should enable simpler API integrations.  After an upcomming announcement of a grace period of 180 days, the legacy types as well as the v1 APIs will be deprecated.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-06\nValid as Of: 2025-02-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1466 ---\nComponent: Data Attribute Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Calibration Improvements\nDescription: We've enhanced the calibration of classification models. The returned probabilities are now more robust and reliable.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-06\nValid as Of: 2025-02-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1467 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Client Passcode Policy\nDescription: (Version 2501) We have introduced two new passcode policies and enhanced the Biometric Authentication properties:   Passcode Reuse Restriction  Digits Only property  Changes to Biometric Authentication Allowed property    For more information, see Defining Client Password Policy and Shared Device Overview (Multiple User Mode).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-06\nValid as Of: 2025-02-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1468 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Simplify Application Overview\nDescription: (Version 2501) We have reorganized the admin UI to group tasks by roles, allowing Developers and Admins to navigate quickly through the application configuration overview page.  For more information, see Application Administration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-06\nValid as Of: 2025-02-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1469 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support service key with external certificate\nDescription: (Version 2501) You can create Service Keys using two new Types:  The original type is renamed as X.509 with SAP managed certificate  X.509 with self-managed certificate is new type    For more information, see Service Keys.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-06\nValid as Of: 2025-02-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1470 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Token Validation Period\nDescription: (Version 2501) Users can configure the Token Validation Period property. The value must be greater than 0 and less than 1440.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-06\nValid as Of: 2025-02-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_63f6b351f7ffd2d9f52dadc6cd593e7ff65a9e3d6487ee6af9c2f6dd88428967_v2"}